#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems and reduced states"
msgstr "Sistem ganda dan state tereduksi"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll turn our attention to how density matrices work for multiple "
"systems, including examples of different types of correlations they can "
"express and how they can be used to describe the states of isolated parts of"
" compound systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan beralih ke cara kerja matriks densitas untuk sistem "
"ganda, termasuk contoh berbagai jenis korelasi yang bisa mereka ekspresikan "
"dan bagaimana mereka bisa digunakan untuk mendeskripsikan state dari bagian-"
"bagian terisolasi dari sistem majemuk.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems {#multiple-systems}"
msgstr "Sistem ganda {#multiple-systems}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices can represent states of multiple systems in an analogous way to state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information, following the same basic idea that multiple systems can be viewed as if they're single, compound systems.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the rows and columns of density matrices representing states of multiple systems are placed in correspondence with the Cartesian product of the classical state sets of the individual systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks densitas bisa merepresentasikan state dari beberapa sistem dengan cara yang analog dengan vektor state dalam formulasi sederhana informasi kuantum, mengikuti ide dasar yang sama bahwa beberapa sistem bisa dipandang seolah-olah merupakan sistem tunggal yang majemuk.\n"
"Dalam istilah matematis, baris dan kolom dari matriks densitas yang merepresentasikan state dari beberapa sistem diletakkan berkorespondensi dengan produk Cartesian dari himpunan state klasik dari masing-masing sistem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, recall the state vector representations of the four Bell "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, ingat kembali representasi vektor state dari empat Bell "
"state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representations of these states are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Representasi matriks densitas dari state-state ini adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Product states {#product-states}"
msgstr "Product states {#product-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we had for state vectors, tensor products of density matrices represent *independence* between the states of multiple systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ is prepared in the state represented by the density matrix $\\rho$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ is independently prepared in the state represented by $\\sigma,$ then the density matrix describing the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is the tensor product $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan apa yang kita miliki untuk vektor state, produk tensor dari matriks densitas merepresentasikan *kebebasan* (independence) antara state dari beberapa sistem.\n"
"Misalnya, jika $\\mathsf{X}$ disiapkan dalam state yang direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas $\\rho$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ secara independen disiapkan dalam state yang direpresentasikan oleh $\\sigma,$ maka matriks densitas yang mendeskripsikan state dari $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ adalah produk tensor $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same terminology is used here as in the simplified formulation of "
"quantum information: states of this form are referred to as *product "
"states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terminologi yang sama digunakan di sini seperti dalam formulasi sederhana "
"informasi kuantum: state-state dalam bentuk ini disebut sebagai *product "
"states*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correlated and entangled states {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"
msgstr ""
"State berkorelasi dan state terjalin {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States that cannot be expressed as product states represent *correlations* between systems.\n"
"There are, in fact, different types of correlations that can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Here are a few examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"State yang tidak bisa diekspresikan sebagai product states merepresentasikan *korelasi* antara sistem-sistem.\n"
"Sebenarnya, ada berbagai jenis korelasi yang bisa direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas.\n"
"Berikut beberapa contohnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Correlated classical states.*\n"
"For example, we can express the situation in which Alice and Bob share a random bit like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*State klasik berkorelasi.*\n"
"Misalnya, kita bisa mengekspresikan situasi di mana Alice dan Bob berbagi bit acak seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Ensembles of quantum states.*\n"
"Suppose we have $m$ density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ all representing states of a system $\\mathsf{X},$ and we  randomly choose one of these states according to a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Such a process is represented by an *ensemble* of states, which includes the specification of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ as well as the probabilities $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ We can associate an ensemble of states with a single density matrix, describing both the random choice of $k$ and the corresponding density matrix $\\rho_k,$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ensembel state kuantum.*\n"
"Misalkan kita punya $m$ matriks densitas $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ yang semuanya merepresentasikan state dari suatu sistem $\\mathsf{X},$ dan kita secara acak memilih salah satu state tersebut sesuai dengan vektor probabilitas $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Proses seperti ini direpresentasikan oleh sebuah *ensembel* state, yang mencakup spesifikasi matriks densitas $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ serta probabilitas $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Kita bisa mengaitkan ensembel state dengan satu matriks densitas tunggal, yang mendeskripsikan baik pilihan acak $k$ maupun matriks densitas yang sesuai $\\rho_k,$ seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To be clear, this is the state of a pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ "
"where $\\mathsf{Y}$ represents the classical selection of $k$ — so we're "
"assuming its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ States of this "
"form are sometimes called *classical-quantum states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk jelasnya, ini adalah state dari pasangan "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ di mana $\\mathsf{Y}$ merepresentasikan "
"pemilihan klasik dari $k$ — jadi kita mengasumsikan himpunan state klasiknya"
" adalah $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ State-state dalam bentuk ini kadang disebut "
"*state klasik-kuantum*.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Separable states*. We can imagine situations in which we have a classical "
"correlation among the quantum states of two systems like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*State separabel*. Kita bisa membayangkan situasi di mana ada korelasi "
"klasik di antara state kuantum dari dua sistem seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In words, for each $k$ from $0$ to $m-1,$ we have that with probability "
"$p_k$ the system on the left is in the state $\\rho_k$ and the system on the"
" right is in the state $\\sigma_k.$ States like this are called *separable "
"states*. This concept can also be extended to more than two systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Artinya, untuk setiap $k$ dari $0$ hingga $m-1,$ dengan probabilitas "
"$p_k$ sistem di sebelah kiri berada dalam state $\\rho_k$ dan sistem di "
"sebelah kanan berada dalam state $\\sigma_k.$ State-state seperti ini "
"disebut *state separabel*. Konsep ini juga bisa diperluas ke lebih dari dua "
"sistem.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entangled states*. Not all states of pairs of systems are separable. In the"
" general formulation of quantum information, this is how entanglement is "
"defined: states that are not separable are said to be *entangled*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*State terjalin (entangled)*. Tidak semua state dari pasangan sistem "
"bersifat separabel. Dalam formulasi umum informasi kuantum, begitulah "
"entanglement didefinisikan: state yang tidak separabel dikatakan *terjalin "
"(entangled)*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that this terminology is consistent with the terminology we used in "
"the \"Basics of quantum information\" course. There we said that quantum "
"state vectors that are not product states represent entangled states — and "
"indeed, for any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that is not a "
"product state, we find that the state represented by the density matrix "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is not separable. Entanglement is "
"much more complicated than this for states that are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Perhatikan bahwa terminologi ini konsisten dengan terminologi yang kita "
"gunakan dalam kursus \"Dasar-dasar informasi kuantum\". Di sana kita "
"mengatakan bahwa vektor state kuantum yang bukan product states "
"merepresentasikan state terjalin — dan memang, untuk setiap vektor state "
"kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang bukan product state, kita temukan bahwa "
"state yang direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ tidak separabel. Entanglement jauh "
"lebih rumit dari ini untuk state yang bukan murni (pure).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states and the partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"State tereduksi dan partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a simple but important thing we can do with density matrices in the context of multiple systems, which is to describe the states we obtain by ignoring some of the systems.\n"
"When multiple systems are in a quantum state and we discard or choose to ignore one or more of the systems,\n"
"the state of the remaining systems is called the *reduced state* of those systems.\n"
"Density matrix descriptions of reduced states are easily obtained through a mapping, known as the *partial trace*, from the density matrix describing the state of the whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada hal sederhana namun penting yang bisa kita lakukan dengan matriks densitas dalam konteks sistem ganda, yaitu mendeskripsikan state yang kita peroleh dengan mengabaikan sebagian sistem.\n"
"Ketika beberapa sistem berada dalam state kuantum dan kita membuang atau memilih untuk mengabaikan satu atau lebih sistem,\n"
"state dari sistem-sistem yang tersisa disebut *state tereduksi* dari sistem-sistem tersebut.\n"
"Deskripsi matriks densitas dari state tereduksi mudah diperoleh melalui suatu pemetaan, yang dikenal sebagai *partial trace*, dari matriks densitas yang mendeskripsikan state keseluruhan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: reduced states for an e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh: state tereduksi untuk e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ that are "
"together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan kita punya sepasang qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ yang bersama-"
"sama berada dalam state\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can imagine that Alice holds the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ and Bob holds $\\mathsf{B},$ which is to say that together they share an e-bit.\n"
"We'd like to have a density matrix description of Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, as if Bob decided to take his qubit and visit the stars, never to be seen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa membayangkan Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ dan Bob memegang $\\mathsf{B},$ yang artinya mereka bersama-sama berbagi sebuah e-bit.\n"
"Kita ingin memiliki deskripsi matriks densitas dari qubit Alice $\\mathsf{A}$ secara terpisah, seolah-olah Bob memutuskan untuk membawa qubitnya dan pergi ke bintang-bintang, tak pernah terlihat lagi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First let's think about what would happen if Bob decided somewhere on his journey to measure his qubit with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"If he did this, he would obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama mari kita pikirkan apa yang akan terjadi jika Bob memutuskan di suatu tempat dalam perjalanannya untuk mengukur qubitnya dengan pengukuran basis standar.\n"
"Jika dia melakukannya, dia akan memperoleh hasil $0$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ and he "
"would obtain the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"dalam hal ini state qubit Alice menjadi $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ dan dia akan "
"memperoleh hasil $1$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "dalam hal ini state qubit Alice menjadi $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we ignore Bob's measurement outcome and focus on Alice's qubit, we conclude that she obtains the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with probability $1/2.$\n"
"This leads us to describe the state of Alice's qubit in isolation by the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, jika kita mengabaikan hasil pengukuran Bob dan berfokus pada qubit Alice, kita menyimpulkan bahwa dia memperoleh state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dengan probabilitas $1/2$ dan state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ dengan probabilitas $1/2.$\n"
"Hal ini membuat kita mendeskripsikan state qubit Alice secara terpisah dengan matriks densitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, Alice's qubit is in the completely mixed state.\n"
"To be clear, this description of the state of Alice's qubit doesn't include Bob's measurement outcome; we're ignoring Bob altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, qubit Alice berada dalam state campuran sempurna (completely mixed state).\n"
"Untuk jelasnya, deskripsi state qubit Alice secara terpisah yang baru saja kita peroleh tidak menyertakan hasil pengukuran Bob; kita mengabaikan Bob sepenuhnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it might seem like the density matrix description of Alice's qubit in isolation that we've just obtained relies on the assumption that Bob has measured his qubit, but this is not actually so.\n"
"What we've done is to use the possibility that Bob measures his qubit to argue that the completely mixed state arises as the state of Alice's qubit, based on what we've already learned.\n"
"Of course, nothing says that Bob must measure his qubit — but nothing says that he doesn't.\n"
"And if he's light years away, then nothing he does or doesn't do can possibly influence the state of Alice's qubit viewed it in isolation.\n"
"That is to say, the description we've obtained for the state of Alice's qubit is the only description consistent with the impossibility of faster-than-light communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, mungkin terasa seolah deskripsi matriks densitas dari qubit Alice secara terpisah yang baru saja kita peroleh bergantung pada asumsi bahwa Bob telah mengukur qubitnya, tetapi sebenarnya tidak begitu.\n"
"Yang kita lakukan adalah menggunakan kemungkinan Bob mengukur qubitnya untuk berargumen bahwa state campuran sempurna muncul sebagai state qubit Alice, berdasarkan apa yang sudah kita pelajari.\n"
"Tentu saja, tidak ada yang mengharuskan Bob mengukur qubitnya — tetapi tidak ada yang mengatakan dia tidak melakukannya.\n"
"Dan jika dia berada bertahun-tahun cahaya jauhnya, maka apapun yang dia lakukan atau tidak lakukan tidak mungkin mempengaruhi state qubit Alice yang dipandang secara terpisah.\n"
"Artinya, deskripsi yang kita peroleh untuk state qubit Alice adalah satu-satunya deskripsi yang konsisten dengan ketidakmungkinan komunikasi lebih cepat dari cahaya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider the state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ which happens to be the completely mixed state as well.\n"
"Indeed, for all four Bell states we find that the reduced state of both Alice's qubit and Bob's qubit is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga bisa mempertimbangkan state dari qubit Bob $\\mathsf{B},$ yang kebetulan juga merupakan state campuran sempurna.\n"
"Memang, untuk keempat Bell state kita temukan bahwa state tereduksi dari qubit Alice maupun qubit Bob adalah state campuran sempurna.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states for a general quantum state vector {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"
msgstr ""
"State tereduksi untuk vektor state kuantum umum {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's generalize the example just discussed to two arbitrary systems $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ not necessarily qubits in the state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"We'll assume the classical state sets of $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are $\\Sigma$ and $\\Gamma,$ respectively.\n"
"A density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the combined system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ therefore has row and column indices corresponding to the Cartesian product $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita generalisasi contoh yang baru saja dibahas ke dua sistem arbitrer $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B},$ tidak harus qubit dalam state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Kita akan mengasumsikan himpunan state klasik dari $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B}$ adalah $\\Sigma$ dan $\\Gamma,$ masing-masing.\n"
"Sebuah matriks densitas $\\rho$ yang merepresentasikan state dari sistem gabungan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ karenanya memiliki indeks baris dan kolom yang berkorespondensi dengan produk Cartesian $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that the state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is described by the quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ so the density matrix describing this state is $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"We'll obtain a density matrix description of the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, which is conventionally denoted $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A superscript is also sometimes used rather than a subscript.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan state dari $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ dideskripsikan oleh vektor state kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ sehingga matriks densitas yang mendeskripsikan state ini adalah $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"Kita akan memperoleh deskripsi matriks densitas dari state $\\mathsf{A}$ secara terpisah, yang secara konvensional dinotasikan $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(Superscript juga kadang digunakan daripada subscript.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the form\n"
msgstr "Vektor state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ bisa diekspresikan dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a uniquely determined collection of vectors $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"In particular, these vectors can be determined through a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk kumpulan vektor $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}$ yang ditentukan secara unik.\n"
"Khususnya, vektor-vektor ini bisa ditentukan melalui rumus sederhana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reasoning similarly to the previous example of an e-bit, if we were to "
"measure the system $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement, we would"
" obtain each outcome $b\\in\\Gamma$ with probability "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ in which case the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan alasan yang serupa dengan contoh e-bit sebelumnya, jika kita mengukur"
" sistem $\\mathsf{B}$ dengan pengukuran basis standar, kita akan memperoleh "
"setiap hasil $b\\in\\Gamma$ dengan probabilitas "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ dalam hal ini state dari $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As a density matrix, this state can be written as follows.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai matriks densitas, state ini bisa dituliskan sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Averaging the different states according to the probabilities of the "
"respective outcomes, we arrive at the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan merata-ratakan state-state yang berbeda sesuai probabilitas dari "
"hasil masing-masing, kita sampai pada matriks densitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The formula\n"
msgstr "Rumus\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"leads us to the description of the reduced state of $\\mathsf{A}$ for any "
"density matrix $\\rho$ of the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ not just a "
"pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"membawa kita ke deskripsi state tereduksi $\\mathsf{A}$ untuk sembarang "
"matriks densitas $\\rho$ dari pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ bukan "
"hanya state murni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula must work, simply by linearity together with the fact that "
"every density matrix can be written as a convex combination of pure "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rumus ini pasti berlaku, cukup dengan linearitas bersama fakta bahwa setiap "
"matriks densitas dapat ditulis sebagai kombinasi konveks dari state murni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation being performed on $\\rho$ to obtain $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ in this equation is known as the *partial trace*, and to be more precise we say that the partial trace is performed on $\\mathsf{B},$ or that $\\mathsf{B}$ is *traced out*.\n"
"This operation is denoted $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ so we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi yang dilakukan pada $\\rho$ untuk mendapatkan $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dalam persamaan ini dikenal sebagai *partial trace*, dan lebih tepatnya kita katakan bahwa partial trace dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{B},$ atau bahwa $\\mathsf{B}$ *di-trace out*.\n"
"Operasi ini dinotasikan $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ sehingga kita bisa menulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define the partial trace on $\\mathsf{A},$ so it's the system "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ that gets traced out rather than $\\mathsf{B},$ like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga bisa mendefinisikan partial trace pada $\\mathsf{A},$ sehingga "
"sistem $\\mathsf{A}$ yang di-trace out bukan $\\mathsf{B},$ seperti ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives us the density matrix description $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ of the "
"state of $\\mathsf{B}$ in isolation rather than $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini memberikan kita deskripsi matriks densitas $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ dari "
"state $\\mathsf{B}$ secara terpisah alih-alih $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recapitulate, if $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is any pair of systems and "
"we have a density matrix $\\rho$ describing a state of "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ the *reduced states* of the systems "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk merangkum, jika $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ adalah sembarang pasangan "
"sistem dan kita punya matriks densitas $\\rho$ yang mendeskripsikan state "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ *state tereduksi* dari sistem $\\mathsf{A}$ dan"
" $\\mathsf{B}$ adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho$ is a density matrix, then $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ will also necessarily be density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $\\rho$ adalah matriks densitas, maka $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dan "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ juga pasti akan menjadi matriks densitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These notions can be generalized to any number of systems in place of two in a natural way.\n"
"In general, we can put the names of whatever systems we choose in the subscript of a density matrix $\\rho$ to describe the reduced state of just those systems.\n"
"For example, if $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ and $\\mathsf{C}$ are systems and $\\rho$ is a density matrix describing a state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ then we can define\n"
msgstr ""
"Konsep-konsep ini dapat digeneralisasi ke jumlah sistem berapa pun sebagai pengganti dua sistem dengan cara yang alami.\n"
"Secara umum, kita bisa meletakkan nama sistem apa pun yang kita pilih di subscript matriks densitas $\\rho$ untuk mendeskripsikan state tereduksi hanya dari sistem-sistem tersebut.\n"
"Misalnya, jika $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ dan $\\mathsf{C}$ adalah sistem dan $\\rho$ adalah matriks densitas yang mendeskripsikan state $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ maka kita dapat mendefinisikan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and similarly for other choices for the systems.\n"
msgstr "dan demikian pula untuk pilihan sistem lainnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to describe the partial trace mappings "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ is"
" that they are the *unique* linear mappings that satisfy the formulas\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara alternatif untuk mendeskripsikan pemetaan partial trace "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dan $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ "
"adalah bahwa keduanya merupakan pemetaan linear *unik* yang memenuhi rumus\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these formulas, $N$ and $M$ are square matrices of the appropriate sizes:\n"
"the rows and columns of $M$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{A}$ and the rows and columns of $N$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam rumus-rumus ini, $N$ dan $M$ adalah matriks persegi berukuran yang sesuai:\n"
"baris dan kolom dari $M$ berkorespondensi dengan state klasik $\\mathsf{A}$ dan baris dan kolom dari $N$ berkorespondensi dengan state klasik $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This characterization of the partial trace is not only fundamental from a mathematical viewpoint, but can also allow for quick calculations in some situations.\n"
"For example, consider this state of a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Karakterisasi partial trace ini bukan hanya fundamental dari sudut pandang matematika, tetapi juga memungkinkan perhitungan cepat dalam beberapa situasi.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, pertimbangkan state pasangan qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute the reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ for instance, we can use linearity together with the fact that\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ and $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ have unit trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menghitung state tereduksi $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ misalnya, kita dapat menggunakan linearitas bersama fakta bahwa\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ dan $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ memiliki trace satuan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ can be computed similarly.\n"
msgstr "State tereduksi $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ dapat dihitung dengan cara serupa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"
msgstr "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partial trace can also be described explicitly in terms of matrices.\n"
"Here we'll do this just for two qubits, but this can also be generalized to larger systems.\n"
"Assume that we have two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ so that any density matrix describing a state of these two qubits can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Partial trace juga dapat dideskripsikan secara eksplisit dalam bentuk matriks.\n"
"Di sini kita akan melakukan ini hanya untuk dua qubit, tetapi ini juga bisa digeneralisasi ke sistem yang lebih besar.\n"
"Anggap kita punya dua qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ sehingga setiap matriks densitas yang mendeskripsikan state dua qubit ini dapat ditulis sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some choice of complex numbers $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"
msgstr "untuk suatu pilihan bilangan kompleks $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace over the first system has the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Partial trace atas sistem pertama memiliki rumus berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to think about this formula begins by viewing $4\\times 4$ matrices as $2\\times 2$ block matrices, where each block is $2\\times 2.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara untuk memahai rumus ini dimulai dengan memandang matriks $4\\times 4$ sebagai matriks blok $2\\times 2,$ di mana setiap blok berukuran $2\\times 2.$\n"
"Yaitu,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then have\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudian punya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the formula when the second system is traced out rather than the "
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah rumusnya ketika sistem kedua yang di-trace out alih-alih "
"sistem pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In terms of block matrices of a form similar to before, we have this "
"formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bentuk matriks blok yang serupa dengan sebelumnya, kita punya rumus "
"ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The block matrix descriptions of these functions can be extended to systems "
"larger than qubits in a natural and direct way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Deskripsi matriks blok dari fungsi-fungsi ini dapat diperluas ke sistem yang"
" lebih besar dari qubit dengan cara yang alami dan langsung.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To finish the lesson, let's apply these formulas to the same state we "
"considered above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengakhiri pelajaran ini, mari kita terapkan rumus-rumus ini pada "
"state yang sama yang kita pertimbangkan di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state of the first system $\\mathsf{A}$ is\n"
msgstr "State tereduksi dari sistem pertama $\\mathsf{A}$ adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the reduced state of the second system $\\mathsf{B}$ is\n"
msgstr "dan state tereduksi dari sistem kedua $\\mathsf{B}$ adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
